#
# File:         sdkconfig.defaults.g4848
# Module:       Build / ESP-IDF defaults, Guition ESP32-4848S040 layer
#
# Purpose:      What the Guition ESP32-4848S040 build changes from
#               sdkconfig.defaults and sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3.
#               platformio.ini names this file for the board's environments
#               through SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS (board_build.cmake_extra_args).
#               IDF 5.3.1 still reads "<file>.<target>" after each file it is
#               given (tools/cmake/kconfig.cmake), so the order is
#               sdkconfig.defaults, sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, then this
#               file, and a later value wins.
#
#               The part: ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8, 8 MB octal PSRAM, the S3
#               layer's own. What this board changes: the console (a CH340 on
#               UART0, the chip's USB pins being the panel's and the touch
#               controller's), and what an RGB panel needs, as on the 4.3B.
#               Sources in src/board.h, BBS_BOARD_GT_4848S040.
#
#               PlatformIO keeps the generated sdkconfig.<env>, a value it
#               already holds wins over this file, and it does not watch this
#               file: delete sdkconfig.guition_4848s040* after editing here,
#               and check the generated file. A value outside its Kconfig
#               range is discarded, not clamped.
#
# Targets:      ESP32-S3 (ESP-IDF 5.3.1)
# See also:     sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3, sdkconfig.defaults.ws43b,
#               platformio.ini, src/board.h
#
